 "text": "Clinical\nCan enable faster decisions on discharge and admission\nMay improve diagnosis of MI in women\nAids in faster, more accurate diagnosis of MI\nAnalytical\nImproved precision\nImproved sensitivity\nFinancial\nCan minimize unnecessary procedures and tests\nMay reduce costs, length of stay, admissions rates and overnight stays\nChallenge\nThe burden of heart disease and mi\n6 - 8m\n6-8 million people present to US Emergency Departments every year with suspected Myocardial Infarction (MI). 3\n8-15%\nOnly 8-15% are having an MI so, in theory, the majority could be discharged. 4\nRapidly diagnosing and triaging chest pain patients\nEmergency departments continually face the challenge of rapidly diagnosing and triaging patients with chest pain. 5\nBiomarkers can help clarify the clinical picture. Timely action on cardiac laboratory results is critical and may improve patient outcomes. 6\nAbbott’s high-sensitivity troponin I meets ifcc criteria\nIfcc definition of hs-ctn assay 7\nFor an assay to be considered a high-sensitivity troponin assay, the following criteria should be met:\nTotal imprecision at the 99th percentile value should be <10% CV.\nMeasurable concentrations below the 99th percentile should be attainable with an assay at a concentration value above the assay’s limit of detection (LoD) for at least 50% of healthy men and women.\nAlinity i hs t n i_STAT 8 ARCHITECT hs T n I_STAT 9\n99 th percentile CV at medical decision points % of people detected at ≥LoD 10 99 th percentile CV at medical decision points % of peope detected at ≥LoD 10\nFemale 14 ng/L 2.7% at 13.9 ng/L 63.4% 17 ng/L 5.0% 54.12%\nMale 35 ng/L 2.0% at 36.9 ng/L 87.3% 35ng/L 4.1% 77.42%\nOverall 27 ng/L 3.3% at 20.3 ng/L 75.3% 28 ng/L 4.3% 65.77%\nPercent healthy individuals detected by troponin assays\n>50% OF HEALTHY MALES AND FEMALES HAVE DETECTABLE VALUES (ABOVE THE L o D)\n% measurable values > l o d\nAdapted from Apple FS, et al. Clin Chem 58(11):1574-1581\nFor In Vitro Diagnostic Use\nIntended use\nThe Alinity i and ARCHITECT STAT High-Sensitivity Troponin-I assays are chemiluminescent microparticle immunoassays (CMIA) used for the quantitative determination of cardiac troponin I (cTnI) in human plasma (lithium heparin on Alinity i or dipotassium {K2} edta on ARCHITECT) on the Alinity i and ARCHITECT systems.\nThe Alinity i and ARCHITECT STAT High Sensitivity Troponin-I assays are to be used as an aid in the diagnosis of myocardial infarction (MI).\nClick here to view important safety information\nAha/acc clinical guidelines 11\n“high-sensitivity c T n is preferred because it allows rapid detection of myocardial injury and has increased diagnostic accuracy”\nUnderstand the value of high-sensitivity troponin video\nUs customer testimonial video\nHeart partnership program\nLet's talk\nContact your Abbott representative to learn more.\nRequest more info\nExplore\nKnowledge Center\nFind the latest information in laboratory science, therapeutic areas and Abbott innovation.\nVisit the Knowledge Center\nCustomer Portal\nReceive exclusive benefits and resources when you register to access to the Customer Portal.\nRegister now\nStay Connected\nSubscribe to Abbott's Core Lab newsletter to stay updated on our latest innovations, product launches, publications and events.",
