{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{
 "url": "https://www.siemens-healthineers.com/en-us/blood-gas/blood-gas-systems/epoc-blood-analysis-system",
 "title": "epoc® Blood Analysis System - Siemens Healthineers USA",
 "text": "Home\nPoint-of-Care Testing\nBlood Gas\nBlood Gas Systems\nepoc® Blood Analysis System\nRaise the benchmark for handheld point of care testing epoc Blood Analysis System with the NXS Host\nHelp improve workflow and the clinical experience with the epoc Blood Analysis System. The epoc System is a handheld, bedside solution that provides lab-accurate blood gas, electrolyte, and metabolite (BGEM) results at the patient’s side in less than 1 minute from sample application.\nThe epoc System consists of three components: the NXS Host mobile computer , the Reader , and the BGEM Test Card . The single-use Test Card has 13 analytes and requires no refrigeration.\nA simple user interface guides the clinician through every step of the testing process. Test results are color coded to clearly distinguish between results that are normal or out of range. Wireless connectivity allows communication directly with other members of the care team.\nFeatures & Benefits Clinical Use Technical Specifications\nFeatures & Benefits\nZoom\nLearn more about the epoc System’s intuitive touchscreen interface; enhanced security with Android 9.0 OS; and streamlined testing workflow through the resources below.\nBrochure: epoc System – Time and Cost Comparison\nepoc System Components: NXS Host, Reader, Test Card\nFAQs: epoc Blood Analysis System\nSlide Show: Optimizing your Workflow\nSlide Show: epoc System and the Continuum of Care\nWhite Paper: Summary of Analytical Methods and Performance (pdf) 1.77 MB\nWhite Paper: POC Blood Analysis – Accurate, Quality Testing (pdf) 3.34 MB\nVideo Demonstrations\nVideo Overview\nClick the topics below to learn more about the epoc System’s Features and Benefits\nImprove quality assurance with bar coded test cards and automated expiration checks\nHealthcare providers spend more time with the patient to drive faster diagnosis and treatment decisions.\nZoom\nThe epoc System helps improve quality assurance with the following features:\nEnables you to be where patients need you most (bedside)\nPatient-side testing simplifies the process, eliminating sample transport and pre-analytical sample degradation to provide accurate results\nSecure, wireless connection to confirm real-time patient identification to mitigate data entry and transcription errors\nEasy access to room temperature stable test cards at the patient’s side\nResults can be available in less than 1 minute and accurately reflect patient’s immediate condition\nConnects the entire team, so it doesn’t matter if lab staff and caregivers work in different parts of the hospital\nAccelerate clinical decision making with accurate and actionable results in less than one minute\nActionable results in less than 1 minute at the patient's side.\nResults reflect that patient's immediate condition, not their condition 30 minutes ago.\nPrev\nInsert test card.\nScan patient ID.\nDraw blood sample.\nInject blood sample.\nRead results.\nNext\nSimplify inventory management with room temperature stable test cards\nThe laboratory spends less time on complex inventory management optimizing time and resource utilization.\nZoom\nThe Benefits of a Single Room Temperature Barcoded Test Card:\nEnable patient-centered care\nStreamline inventory management\nEliminate manual tracking of reagents\nAutomate quality assurance\nEliminate the risk of running expired reagents\nFurther mitigate risk of diagnosis and treatment based on erroneous results\nConnected comprehensive care with secure wireless connectivity and POC Informatics Solutions\nLeverage centralized control of decentralized testing with secure, wireless communication and our POC Informatics Solutions\nThe epoc system provides bidirectional communication with POCcelerator data manager, allowing caregivers the ability for device, operator and inventory management, along with quality control. This provides the ability to proactively manage data across the hospital, giving you centralized control over decentralized testing.\nConnected Comprehensive Care\nManage, configure, control, and troubleshoot testing on epoc, RAPIDPoint® and RAPIDLab® blood gas systems with our POC Ecosystem™ Solution. Enable the monitoring of information from every connected analyzer, including epoc Blood Analysis Systems and test devices with more than 40 manufacturers, with our POCcelerator Data Management System.\nPOC Ecosystem™ Solution\nWhatever your device mix and wherever critical testing takes place, Siemens Healthineers’ POC Informatics help advance workforce productivity, improve clinical workflows, satisfy compliance and accreditation requirements, and optimize the management of resources.\nTransforming Care Delivery at Huntsville Hospital\nHuntsville Hospital reduced their (sepsis) mortality rate by ~50% as part of a sepsis program.\n“For every hour you wait to give an antibiotic, the mortality for that patient increases 8%, so now that we have the handheld device, the nurse can get those results within 3 minutes, and we know how to treat that patient.” —Carissa Hicks, RN, Huntsville Hospital\nConnectivity with the Enterprise Data Management System (EDM)\nThe Enterprise Data Manager (EDM) software is a powerful and convenient tool to manage patient results wirelessly from the bedside as well as transmitting results into the electronic medical record (EMR).\nAccessible via any networked computer\nManage individual or multiple epoc devices within your network\nHospital compliance and performance reporting\nInventory and Patient data management\nCustomizable critical and reference ranges by sample type (arterial, venous, capillary, etc.)\nAutonomous software upgrades and device management\nClinical Use\nTest results from the epoc® system correlate with leading point-of-care benchtop blood gas and chemistry analyzers.\nDownload Summary of Analytical Methods and Performance (pdf) 2.03 MB\nTechnical Specifications\nClick on the link below to download the epoc® system’s technical specifications.\nepoc Blood Analysis System Technical Specifications (pdf) 0.16 MB\nContact Sales\nDid this information help you?\nYes No\nThank you.\nWould you like to provide detailed feedback?\n125 / 125\nCancel Send\nThe products/features shown on this webpage are not commercially available in all countries. Due to regulatory reasons, their future availability cannot be guaranteed. Please contact your local Siemens Healthineers organization for further details.",
 "truncated": false,
