ion Report .................................................... 42 \nA. Executive Summary........................................................................................ 42 \nB. MDUFA Review Goals ................................................................................... 45 \n1. FY 2025 Review Goal Performance Results .............................................. 46 \n2. FY 2024 Review Goal Performance Results (Updated)............................... 47 \n3. FY 2023 Review Goal Performance Results (Updated)............................... 48 \nC. MDUFA Performance Enhancement Goals ....................................................... 50 \n1. Infrastructure and Program and Process Implementation........................... 50 \nVI. Appendix E: Rationale for MDUFA Program Changes  ......................................... 52 \nA. Changes in the Number of Individuals Hired as Agreed in the MDUFA V \nCommitment Letter, the Number of Remaining Vacancies, the Number of Full-Time \nEquivalents (FTEs) Funded by Fees Collected Pursuant to Section 738, and the \nNumber of FTEs Funded by BA by Division Within CDRH, CBER, OII, and OC. 52 \n1. Changes in the Number of Indivi\n\n[Content truncated]",
