 "modules": {
  "analogs": "LumiraDx (cautionary, 2021-2024): listed at a $3.0B de-SPAC valuation after cutting the deal from $5.0B and sold its point-of-care technology to Roche for $295M after lenders took control — a multi-assay platform with revenue still went for a fifth of its listing value. Cue Health (cautionary, 2021-2024): raised $480M+ and reached a $2.3B valuation, then filed Chapter 7 in 2024 after an FDA warning letter on unauthorised device changes and lot-release failures — the closest precedent to Vantelle's quality-system gap. QuidelOrtho-LEX Diagnostics (pricing, 2026): $100M cash for a platform already cleared and CLIA-waived, the current clearing price for the asset Vantelle will hold in 2028. Truvian Sciences (cautionary, 2015-2026): raised $294M, cleared 12 analytes by 2026-01-12 and remains private eleven years after founding — the base rate for finger-stick platforms reaching commercial scale late and at a discount. The decision rule: a cleared, waived, revenue-generating point-of-care platform transacts at $100-300M in this market, so entry must leave room for a 3x return below that band.",
