   "early_warning": "First principal payment on $5.0M in 2027-04 plus a clearance slip; working capital above $5M in 2028."
  }
 ],
 "consensus": {
  "consensus": "The company and the $140M pre-money assume 8 panels per analyzer-day, a Q1 2027 clearance, a 2027 CLIA waiver, $78.5M of 2029 revenue and a point-of-care market of $2.4B; the insider $8M commitment implies existing investors accept that timeline. Every reimbursement calculation in the plan uses 2026 CLFS rates, before the preliminary CY2027 Chemistry cut [S149].",
  "our_view": "The need is real and the packaging lead is genuine for 12-24 months, but the plan is priced as if clearance, waiver, 8-panel utilisation and 2026 reimbursement all hold. We would invest only at $60-80M pre-money, with the Series A participation capped, the $30M tranched on clearance and the Corvia terms cleaned up; at $140M the evidence supports waiting.",
  "evidence": "The deck's own operating data contradict the utilisation assumption: 1,680 cartridges a month across 55 analyzers is 1.22 per operating day, a 6.5x gap, and at that rate the same 13,200 sites and $38 price support $368M, not $2.4B [S1, S79]. FDA's clocks put a Q3 2027 waiver filing into 2028, and no troponin-I system appears on the waived list [S72, S104, S145]. The 2026 clearing price for a cleared, waived platform was $100M [S126]. CMS's preliminary CY2027 fee schedule cuts Chemistry rates 16%, taking the clinic's margin per cartridge from $37.98 to $10.43 on a 15% path [S149].",
