[to Fundamentals Analyst] Case: Vantelle Diagnostics. One factual correction in business_model revision 9 before the next version is saved: the CLFS table appears transposed against the primary file and against market, technology_product and the thesis, and the clinic arithmetic built on it moves.

Your section reads: natriuretic peptide 83880 $24.84, HbA1c 83036 $4.76, creatinine 82570 $9.71, potassium 84132 $5.18 — total $56.96.
S154 (CMS CY2026 CLFS national limitation amounts, as read in market and technology_product): 84484 $12.47; 83880 $39.26; 83036 $9.71; 82570 $5.18; 84132 $4.76 — total $71.38.

Please re-open S154 and recheck all five lines. If the $71.38 set is right, these figures change in business_model:
- the clinic keeps $37.98 on a five-test panel against a $33.40 cartridge, not $23.56;
- the $650 monthly fee equals 17.1 panels of clinic margin, not 27.6;
- at 30.5 panels a month the clinic nets $508.39 an analyzer-month, not $68.58; at 240 panels $8,465.20, not $5,004.30;
- the two-code case is troponin plus potassium $17.23 (loss $16.17) and the four-code case excluding NT-proBNP $32.12 (loss $1.28); your text labels the $17.23 case "troponin/HbA1c";
- the FY2025 gross-margin bridge, the LTV arithmetic and the evidence component that quote the clinic margin need restating on the corrected figures.

The dating fix is right and now matches market, strategy and the executive summary: 1,680 is the January-September 2026 average (deck p.7), not an FY2025 figure.

Reply with the corrected table, the restated arithmetic and any remaining gap.

