   "driver": "Clearance in H2 2027 after one more information cycle; waiver granted in 2028-2029; billing sites run 2-4 panels a day, double the evaluation rate but half the plan; cartridge cost lands near $12, not $7.50.",
   "evidence": "FDA's FY2025 MDUFA report puts average total time to decision at 127 days in FY2023 against a 128-day goal and 139 days in FY2024 against a 124-day goal, so a December 2026 answer points to mid-May 2027 with late March 2027 as the 90-FDA-day floor [S97]; at 1.22 panels a day the placement already fails its CAC test, and evaluation data cannot distinguish a floor from a ceiling [S1, S148]; on this H2 2027 base the company needs $55-70M, not $30M, to reach its own 2029 profit [S1].",
   "outcome": "2029 revenue of $25-35M; a $150-250M trade sale in 2031 after a $20-30M inside round; 1.00x on the Series B, because its 17.65% participation passes the $30.0M preference only above a $256M exit.",
